{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>Kissing</b> — with a lamed, by hand or shoulder or neck; without a lamed, by mouth." "<b>וַיָרַח.</b> With patach on the resh because of the following nun. So too \"וַיָנַע לבבו\" (Isaiah 7:2), \"וַיָנַח בכל גבול מצרים\" (Exodus 10:15), and all of them are from the second [binyan] seen [forms]." "<b>See.</b> Speech with the heart. And there was a good fragrance in the garments, just as he thought in his heart that he was Esau coming from the field. He smelled his garments like the fragrance of the blossoms of the trees, for it is possible that this deed was in the first month."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:01.352460854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}